# Contribution and PR Rules

When preparing or reviewing changes for Waypoint Queue:

## Pull request requirements

- **Related Issue**: Link to the issue the change relates to. For enhancements without an issue, follow [suggesting an enhancement](https://github.com/PrinceOfPluto/WaypointQueue/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#suggesting-enhancements). For bug fixes without an issue, follow [reporting a bug](https://github.com/PrinceOfPluto/WaypointQueue/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#reporting-bugs).
- **Endorsement**: The change must be endorsed by a maintainer before submission.
- **Template**: Fill out every section of the PR template. Incomplete PRs may be closed at maintainers' discretion.

## Required PR sections

1. **Description of the Change** – Explain the design so a reviewer unfamiliar with the code can understand what the code does.
2. **Alternatives Considered** – What other approaches were considered and why this one was chosen.
3. **Possible Drawbacks** – Side effects, user impact, backwards compatibility with saves.
4. **Verification Process** – How you verified new and changed behavior and that no regressions were introduced (steps and results).

When editing or suggesting PR text, ensure these sections are present and substantive.

## Git commit messages

- Use **present tense** ("Add feature" not "Added feature").
- Use **imperative mood** ("Move cursor to..." not "Moves cursor to...").
- Limit the **first line to 72 characters** or less.
- Reference issues and pull requests liberally **after the first line**.
